---
title: "max_withdraw_amount (Scallop Sui Lending Protocol)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_collateral: collateral_amount = obligation::collateral(obligation, coin_type)
    q_get_collateral --> q_calc_debts: debts_value = debts_value_usd_with_weight(obligation, ...)
    q_calc_debts --> q_check_no_debt: debts_value == 0
    q_check_no_debt --> q_return_all: no debt
    q_check_no_debt --> q_calc_available: has debt
    q_return_all --> [*]: return collateral_amount
    q_calc_available --> q_get_price: available_borrow = collaterals_value - debts_value (if positive)
    q_get_price --> q_calc_withdraw: available_withdraw = available_borrow / coin_price * coin_scale
    q_calc_withdraw --> q_get_cf: collateral_factor = risk_model::collateral_factor
    q_get_cf --> q_check_cf_zero: collateral_factor == 0
    q_check_cf_zero --> q_return_cf_zero: collateral_factor is zero
    q_check_cf_zero --> q_apply_cf: collateral_factor > 0
    q_return_cf_zero --> q_check_available_positive: available_borrow > 0
    q_check_available_positive --> q_return_all_cf0: yes, other collateral covers debt
    q_check_available_positive --> q_return_zero: no, cannot withdraw
    q_return_all_cf0 --> [*]: return collateral_amount
    q_return_zero --> [*]: return 0
    q_apply_cf --> [*]: return min(available_withdraw / collateral_factor, collateral_amount)

    note right of q_calc_available
        INV-001: available_borrow = max(0, collaterals_value_for_borrow - debts_value_weighted)
        INV-002: withdrawal limited to maintain overcollateralization
    end note

    note right of q_apply_cf
        INV-003: collateral_factor adjusts raw withdrawal amount for risk
        INV-004: zero collateral_factor means asset has no borrowing power
    end note
